2026-09-27T07:58:25.3960891Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3961193Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3961650Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3962064Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3962195Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3962499Z ================
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3962676Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3962941Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3963602Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3963930Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3964084Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3964463Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3964763Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3964969Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3965531Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3966057Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3967167Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3968317Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3968490Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3969211Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3970092Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3970562Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3971063Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3971811Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3971964Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3972303Z ========
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3972506Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3974731Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3977094Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3977645Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3978466Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3979664Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3980704Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3981683Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3982463Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3983156Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3983339Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:58:25.3983737Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:58:25.4065023Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:25.4066940Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:58:25.4069013Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:25.4070043Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:58:25.4071412Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:58:25.4071740Z 
